microscopy study of MSI-78 in lipid bilayers</article-title><source>Biophys J</source><year>2005</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>4043</fpage><lpage>4050</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16183881</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1529/biophysj.105.062596</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allende</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Simon</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>McIntosh</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Melittin-induced bilayer leakage depends on lipid material properties: evidence for toroidal pores</article-title><source>Biophys J</source><year>2005</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>1828</fpage><lpage>1837</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15596510</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1529/biophysj.104.049817</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roumestand</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Louis</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Aumelas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Grassy</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Calas</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Chavanieu</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oligomerization of protegrin-1 in the presence of DPC micelles. A proton high-resolution NMR study</article-title><source>FEBS Lett</source><year>1998</year><volume>421</volume><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>267</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9468319</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0014-5793(97)01579-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buffy</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Waring</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lehrer</surname><given-names>RI</given-names></name><name><surname>Hong</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Immobilization and aggregation of the antimicrobial peptide protegrin-1 in lipid bilayers investigated by solid-state NMR</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>2003</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>13725</fpage><lpage>13734</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14622019</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/bi035187w</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buffy</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Waring</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hong</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Determination of peptide oligomerization in lipid bilayers using 19F spin diffusion NMR</article-title><source>J Am Chem Soc</source><year>2005</year><volume>127</volume><fpage>4477</fpage><lpage>4483</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15783230</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/ja043621r</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tang</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Waring</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hong</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intermolecular packing and alignment in an ordered b-hairpin antimicrobial peptide aggregate from 2D solid-state NMR</article-title><source>J Am Chem Soc</source><year>2005</year><volume>127</volume><fpage>13919</fpage><lpage>13927</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16201813</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/ja0526665</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mani</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><